3. MUTANTS -- 9/10 handlers.go sites + dailyAvg/historicalDaily in
   trends.go + both formatter belts KILLED; two survivors examined:
   - handlers.go `spend` (line 1160, budget-vs-actual walk): SURVIVES,
     reconfirmed provably unobservable -- `running += monthTarget - spend`
     absorbs the sign bit unconditionally (verified in Go:
     `monthTarget-(+0) == monthTarget-(-0)` bit-for-bit for any nonzero
     monthTarget, and `spend` has no other consumer in the function).
     Matches attempt 1's proof; still the CB7 precedent for an accepted
     unobservable site.
   - trends.go `spentSoFar` (line 339): mutant SURVIVES the full shipped
     suite (dailyAvg/historicalDaily's mutants ARE killed by
     TestCalculateSpendingVelocity_CancellingWindowIsPositiveZero; this
     one is not, because that test's fixture makes `dailyAvg` (the OTHER
     addend in `monthProjection := spentSoFar + dailyAvg*daysRemaining`)
     exactly +0, and +0 always absorbs ±0 regardless of daysRemaining).
     Investigated whether this is "provably unobservable" like `spend`:
     it is NOT algebraically guaranteed -- computed in Go that when
     `dailyAvg` is a genuine negative (refund-dominant) value AND
     `daysRemaining==0` (last calendar day of a month), `dailyAvg*0` is
     IEEE -0, and `-0(mutant spentSoFar) + -0 = -0`, which
     `json.Marshal` renders as literal `-0` in `month_projection`.
     Traced every consumer of `MonthProjection`: the HTML surfaces
     (insights.html, insights-verdict-bar.html) route through
     `formatMoney`, which already has the CB7 -0 belt and clears the sign
     bit regardless of source -- immune. The one RAW JSON surface,
     `handleVelocityPartial`'s `else` branch (nil-renderer fallback,
     internal/handlers/insights/handlers.go:410-441), would leak it
     verbatim -- but `cmd/server/main.go:112` is the only production call
     site and always passes a non-nil renderer, so that branch is dead in
     every shipped binary today; the branch exists purely for the test
     harness's own "nil renderer triggers fallback paths" convention used
     throughout this codebase. Deterministically testing the
     daysRemaining==0 window would require injecting `time.Now()` into
     `SpendingVelocity` (it is hard-coded today), a refactor beyond CB9's
     declared scope, not a one-line assertion add. Per the constitution's
     own instruction to verify a FAIL's remedy actually repairs something
     real: the shipped SOURCE FIX at spentSoFar is correct and complete;
     what's missing is regression coverage for a scenario that is both
     currently dead code and non-trivial to pin without an out-of-scope
     clock-injection change. Recorded as an observation (coverage gap),
     not a FAIL ground -- distinct from attempt 1's chart-walk gap, which
     was a straightforward missing HTTP test on a live, reachable
     surface.
   - Both formatNumber/formatPercent -0 belts: mutant (belt removed)
